    <fr:title text="Cut in the Syntactic Calculus">Cut in the Syntactic Calculus</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <fr:p>If <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T \to  x]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U , x , V \to  y]]></fr:tex> then <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U , T , V \to  y]]></fr:tex>.

Gentzen's theorem shows that this rule does not increase the expressivity of the deductive system.</fr:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
